{"title":"questing for the grail, sagitarrius i","link":"https://keningzhu.com/journal/questing-for-the-grail-sagitarrius-i","date":1765999387000,"content":"<figure>\n          \n        \n        \n\n        \n          \n            \n          \n            \n                \n                \n                \n                \n                \n                \n                \n                <img src=\"https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/f0177e0d-8a8a-428f-ae5a-d25c1d789d6b/sag+i.png?format=1000w\" width=\"3840\" height=\"2160\" srcset=\"https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/f0177e0d-8a8a-428f-ae5a-d25c1d789d6b/sag+i.png?format=100w 100w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/f0177e0d-8a8a-428f-ae5a-d25c1d789d6b/sag+i.png?format=300w 300w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/f0177e0d-8a8a-428f-ae5a-d25c1d789d6b/sag+i.png?format=500w 500w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/f0177e0d-8a8a-428f-ae5a-d25c1d789d6b/sag+i.png?format=750w 750w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/f0177e0d-8a8a-428f-ae5a-d25c1d789d6b/sag+i.png?format=1000w 1000w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/f0177e0d-8a8a-428f-ae5a-d25c1d789d6b/sag+i.png?format=1500w 1500w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/f0177e0d-8a8a-428f-ae5a-d25c1d789d6b/sag+i.png?format=2500w 2500w\" loading=\"lazy\" />\n\n            \n          \n        \n          \n        \n\n        \n      \n        </figure>\n      \n\n    \n  \n\n\n  \n\n\n \n\n\n  <p><em>this series is created for my collaboration with </em><a href=\"https://www.ceremony-studio.co.uk/\" target=\"_blank\"><em>LJ of Ceremony</em></a><em> for their communal writing practice, </em><a href=\"https://www.ceremony-studio.co.uk/atmospheres\" target=\"_blank\"><em>Atmospheres</em></a><em>, based of the 36 decans of the astrological year. </em></p>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  \n  \n\n\n\n<hr />\n\n\n  <p><strong>Sagitarrius I</strong> — November 22-30<br /><strong>Key themes from LJ</strong> — wildfire, rainbows, ruby slippers<br /><strong>Before this: </strong><a href=\"https://keningonline.squarespace.com/journal/projecting-dream-realities-scorpio-iii\">projecting dream realities, scorpio iii</a><a href=\"https://keningzhu.com/journal/dosing-the-poison-cure-scorpio-ii\"><br /></a><br />*</p><p>for this illustration, I wanted to channel the infectious energy of “the quest\" inherent in Sagitarrius energy — to be moved by sudden sparks of wildfire towards one’s aim or vision, no matter how remote it feels. after the cocooning darkness of Scorpio, Sagitarrius feels full of optimistic, forward momentum. here, we are the hero in our own journeys. there is certainly something waiting for us, something worth a very long, winding, exhausting adventure onwards. </p><p>but what is it? how do we know when we’ve reached the grail? what does success taste like, and what is its aftertaste? how do we keep ourselves from eternal questing, while never reaching the destination? <em>is there even a destination?</em> </p><p><br />in the creative journey, it reminds me to both practice <em>surrendering totally to the moment</em> — being in the spontaneous flow of response and creation — as well as zooming out, every once in a while, to observe the meta-nature of the quest itself. what are the distant mountain peaks that I’m running towards? how do I know once I’ve arrived? can I take a moment to celebrate my arrival?  </p><p>it all requires a lot of stamina. and patience. the journey itself must feel beautiful and brilliant, even in its troubles, or I would’ve long given up by now. </p>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  \n  \n\n\n\n<hr />\n\n\n  <h1>process</h1>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  \n  \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n